    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Yordan Alvarez** (69.67) and **Trea Turner** (67.69) anchor the Zurich Zebras lineup as the clear offensive pillars. **Yordan Alvarez** remains our premier start, boasting an elite 0.443 xwOBA, and while he faces the respectable Tyler Mahle, his projection holds firm. **Trea Turner** gains significant value today batting second against the lefty Zac Thornton; the combination of a favorable order spot and the platoon advantage creates a high-ceiling environment for him to generate counting stats. Simultaneously, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (67.09) is a vital tactical play, as his 14% dynamic platoon boost against the right-handed Chase Burns aligns perfectly with our organizational mandate to emphasize speed in a category where every steal matters. \n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Lars Nootbaar** (54.64), who narrowly missed the starting cut in favor of **Josh Smith** (57.09). While **Lars Nootbaar** benefited from a positive park factor and a strong projected spot at the top of the order, the optimizer preferred the superior dynamic platoon edge of **Josh Smith** against Kumar Rocker. We are keeping a close watch on **Gary Sanchez** and **Christian Yelich**, as their robust scores\u201458.54 and 67.05 respectively\u2014are based on strong park factors; however, the \"Lineup Pending\" status for both creates an inherent volatility risk should they be rested or slotted deeper into the order. We advise monitoring pre-game reports, especially for **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, who faces a high-hold risk against Dustin May, and **Junior Caminero**, whose marginal score of 55.61 reflects the difficulty of facing Ranger Suarez.",
